'''Urdu literature''' ({{langx|ur|{{Nastaliq|ادبیاتِ اُردُو}}}}, {{transliteration|ur|ALA-LC|''“Adbiyāt-i Urdū”''}}) comprises the literary works, written in the [[Urdu language]]. While it tends to be dominated by [[Urdu poetry|poetry]], especially the verse forms of the ''[[Urdu Ghazal|ghazal]]'' ({{Nastaliq|غزل}}) and ''[[nazm]]'' ({{Nastaliq|نظم}}), it has expanded into other styles of writing, including the short story, or ''afsana'' ({{Nastaliq|افسانہ}}). Urdu literature is popular mostly in [[Pakistan]], where Urdu is the [[Languages of Pakistan|national language]], and in [[India]], where it is an [[Eighth Schedule to the Constitution of India|Eighth Schedule language]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=Languages Included in the Eighth Schedule of the Indian Constitution {{!}} Department of Official Language {{!}} Ministry of Home Affairs {{!}} GoI |url=https://rajbhasha.gov.in/en/languages-included-eighth-schedule-indian-constitution |access-date=2026-10-18 |website=rajbhasha.gov.in}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=A Historical Perspective of Urdu {{!}} National Council for Promotion of Urdu Language |url=https://www.urducouncil.nic.in/council/a-historical-perspective-of-urdu |access-date=2026-10-18 |website=www.urducouncil.nic.in}}</ref>

