[[Singapore]] is a [[city-state]] and [[island country]] in [[maritime Southeast Asia]], located at the end of the [[Malayan Peninsula]] between [[Malaysia]] and [[Indonesia]] as well as the [[Straits of Malacca]] and the [[South China Sea]]. It is highly compact and urbanised. As of 2026, Singapore has a total land area of approximately {{convert|744.3|km2}}.<ref name="total area of Singapore">{{cite web |title=Environment – Latest Data |date=12 February 2026|publisher=Singapore Department of Statistics |url=https://www.singstat.gov.sg/find-data/search-by-theme/society/environment/latest-data|access-date=12 February 2026}}</ref> Singapore is separated from Indonesia by the [[Singapore Strait]] and from Malaysia by the [[Straits of Johor]].

Geographically, Singapore comprises its [[Singapore Island|mainland]] and other islands. The mainland of Singapore measures {{convert|50|km}} from east to west and {{convert|27|km}} from north to south with {{convert|193|km}} of coastline. These figures are based on {{convert|2.515|m}} High Water Mark [[Cadastre|cadastral]] survey boundaries.<ref name="Department of Statistics Singapore">{{cite web|title=Yearbook of Statistics Singapore 2017|url=https://data.gov.sg/dataset/total-land-area-of-singapore|publisher=Department of Statistics Singapore|access-date=30 June 2018}}</ref> It has an [[exclusive economic zone]] of {{convert|1067|km2|mi2|0|abbr=on}}.

